.TH "OSTRYA\-EXPORT" "1" "" "ostrya" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ostrya\-export \- Write the tree of a commit as a tar stream, to stdout or to \%\-\-output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ostrya export [OPTIONS] [COMMIT]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write the tree of a commit as a tar stream, to stdout or to \%\-\-output.
.PP
The stream holds the files of the tree and no ostree objects. The root directory is the member \fB\%\&./\fR, and the other member names are relative paths. Ownership is numeric, and each timestamp is the commit timestamp. The extended attributes are \fB\%SCHILY.xattr.*\fR records, which \%\-\-no\-xattrs removes. The first regular file of a content object goes into the stream in full, and each later file of that object is a tar hardlink to it.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fICOMMIT\fR
The commit to export (a checksum or a ref). Required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-xattrs\fR
Emit no extended attributes.
.TP
\fB\-\-subpath\fR \fIPATH\fR
Export only this directory of the commit, as the archive root.
.IP
PATH must name a directory. A file, a symlink, or a path that names nothing is an error. If the option occurs more than once, the last value wins.
.TP
\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fIPATH\fR
Put PATH in front of every member pathname.
.IP
The command adds no separator after PATH, so a PATH that acts as a directory must end in \fB\%/\fR\&. The name of the root member is PATH with a \fB\%/\fR added if PATH does not end in one. The target of a symlink gets no prefix. If the option occurs more than once, the last value wins.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIPATH\fR
Write the archive to PATH, and not to standard output.
.IP
The command opens PATH before it resolves the commit. An existing file is truncated in place, and keeps its inode and its mode. A new file gets mode \%0666, reduced by the umask. If the export fails after the open, PATH stays truncated. If the option occurs more than once, the last value wins.
.PP
The global options are listed in \fBostrya\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBostrya\fR(1)
